  "body": "**Wanted:** machine files for the most common hobby router frames: Carbide 3D Shapeoko (Carbide Motion / grbl), Inventables X-Carve (grbl), and Onefinity (Buildbotics / Masso, to confirm). Each file holds the work area, travel, spindle or router rpm range, controller dialect on an existing post (grbl, grblHAL, LinuxCNC), and the usual zero habit. Data comes from the makers' published specs. A value that can't be confirmed is marked unconfirmed, never guessed. Related: WorkBee #3038, Laguna/RichAuto #1914 / #1915, Mach3 #2482.\n\n**Done means:** each frame is listed with its source for every value, posts a test program through its post, and is pinned by a machine-file test.\n\nAsked by the user (mkinney), 2026-11-20, for hobby router owners (MisterMaker's WorkBee #3038, Mark's router #1907): \"Mark will prob want him for his router, too. So, it is not a let's wait until later issue; the sooner the better, within reason ofc\".\n\nPart of #3066 (findings: https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/3066#issuecomment-7050655107). The clean-room boundary of #3066 applies: no vendor wording, labels, parameter names or dialog flows.",
